# Cycle-7 REPAIR-IN-PLACE PRICING (2026-07-30). ~2M for two rolls.
#
# Why this set and not the full 30: repair-in-place is the ONE lever this cycle
# shipped that is both effective and unpriced. It can only ADD harnesses on legs
# that exhausted `max_attempts` short of `target_successes` — on the 49 capped
# legs it merely substitutes. So the legs below are exactly where its effect can
# appear, and running the other 21 would spend tokens on legs where the change is
# a no-op by construction.
#
# The 11 short leg-instances in the paired runs reduce to these 9 distinct legs:
#   4 FAKE patches (want: extra catches)   — Chart-19, Math-74, Math-68, Math-73
#   5 GOOD patches (want: no new accusations) — Chart-19, Math-73, Time-4,
#     Closure-62, Math-39
#
# THREE questions, answered together:
#   1. How many extra catches does repair buy? Chart-19's fake leg is the
#      headline — its winning rule family provably died at construction, and it
#      is short in BOTH rolls (3 and 4 accepted of 5).
#   2. Does it cause new false accusations on the 5 good patches? This is the
#      pre-registered priced risk, and the only precision content available.
#   3. Does the effect repeat across two rolls? At a measured 27% leg-flip rate,
#      one roll cannot answer this.
#
# READ IT BY EVENTS FIRST: every repaired harness emits a `harness-repair` event.
# Any accusation on a leg that was silent in the pair gets greped for that marker
# BEFORE being attributed to anything else (pre-registered tripwire).
#
# BASELINE to compare against — the same legs in the paired runs:
#   fakes  : Chart-19 FN/FN, Math-74 TP/TP, Math-68 TP, Math-73 FN(A)
#   correct: Chart-19 TN, Math-73 TN(A)/FP(B), Time-4 TN, Closure-62 FP/FP,
#            Math-39 FP(A)/TN(B)
#
# Config matches the pair exactly (-n 5 -m 12) so the numbers are comparable.
MODEL="gpt-5.4"
COMMON="-n 5 -m 12 --fuzz_timeout 20 --verify_timeout 20 --verify_relations --synthesize_relations --replay_relations_on_patched --rule_compile_repair"
CASES=(
  "-c patchfile:/home/code/drr/Patches/Doverfitting/Arja/Chart/patch1-Chart-19-Arja-plausible.patch"
  "-c patchfile:/home/code/drr/Patches/Doverfitting/Arja/Math/patch1-Math-74-Arja-plausible.patch"
  "-c patchfile:/home/code/drr/Patches/Doverfitting/Arja/Math/patch1-Math-68-Arja-plausible.patch"
  "-c patchfile:/home/code/drr/Patches/Doverfitting/ACS/Math/patch1-Math-73-ACS-plausible.patch"
  "-c patchfile:/home/code/drr/Patches/Dcorrect/ACS/Chart/patch1-Chart-19-ACS.patch"
  "-c patchfile:/home/code/drr/Patches/Dcorrect/Arja/Math/patch1-Math-73-Arja.patch"
  "-c patchfile:/home/code/drr/Patches/Dcorrect/Elixir/Time/patch1-Time-4-Elixir.patch"
  "-c patchfile:/home/code/drr/Patches/Dcorrect/Jaid/Closure/patch1-Closure-62-Jaid.patch"
  "-c patchfile:/home/code/drr/Patches/Dcorrect/Arja/Math/patch1-Math-39-Arja.patch"
)
